-# AGCP Phase 11 Payment Hotfix Script Fix
+# Araabi Global Commerce Platform (AGCP)
 
-This patch replaces only `scripts/repair-phase11-payment-hotfix1.ps1`.
+AGCP is a tenant-aware enterprise commerce and SaaS platform built as an event-driven modular monolith. It combines identity and access control, double-entry wallets, commerce, supplier routing, rules and fraud controls, SaaS entitlements, analytics, payments, notifications, support, reporting, and reliability operations in one deployable system.
 
-It fixes the Windows PowerShell parser error caused by placing a colon immediately after `$LASTEXITCODE` inside an interpolated string.
+## Technology stack
 
-Apply the file over the existing project and run:
+- Laravel 13 and PHP 8.4
+- Next.js 16, React 19, and TypeScript 5.9
+- MySQL 8.4
+- Redis 8
+- Nginx
+- Docker Compose
+
+## Core capabilities
+
+- Multi-tenant request resolution, memberships, roles, and permissions
+- Fortify and Sanctum authentication, email verification, 2FA, passkeys, sessions, devices, and API tokens
+- Double-entry wallet ledger, deposits, holds, adjustments, and refunds
+- Product catalog, variants, prices, inventory, carts, checkout, and order lifecycle
+- Supplier routing, health scoring, failover, polling, and refund orchestration
+- Versioned rules, fraud assessments, dynamic pricing, and manual review
+- SaaS subscriptions, feature entitlements, usage limits, branding, domains, and approved plugins
+- Deterministic analytics, forecasts, customer segments, supplier recommendations, and AI insights
+- Provider-neutral payment intents, signed webhooks, refunds, and reconciliation
+- Notifications, outbound webhooks, support tickets, operations snapshots, and incidents
+- Tax profiles, immutable invoices, exports, scheduled reports, encrypted backups, and restore drills
+
+## Local development
+
+1. Copy the example environment file:
+
+   ```powershell
+   Copy-Item .env.example .env
+   ```
+
+2. Replace every `CHANGE_ME` value in `.env`.
+
+3. Start the development stack:
+
+   ```powershell
+   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d --build
+   ```
+
+4. Run migrations and seed the initial tenant and administrator:
+
+   ```powershell
+   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.dev.yml exec -T backend php artisan migrate --force
+   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.dev.yml exec -T backend php artisan db:seed --class=DatabaseSeeder --force
+   ```
+
+5. Open the application at `http://localhost:8080`.
+
+## Verification
 
 ```powershell
-cd C:\Projects\agcp
 Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process Bypass -Force
-.\scripts\repair-phase11-payment-hotfix1.ps1
+.\scripts\verify-phase13-15.ps1
 ```
+
+The verification suite covers backend regression tests, frontend lint and type checking, health probes, UAT smoke checks, load smoke checks, production configuration checks, and release readiness.
+
+## Production preparation
+
+Use `.env.production.example` as the production template. Do not commit `.env`, credentials, generated keys, database dumps, or backup archives.
+
+Production deployment guidance is available in:
+
+- `docs/PHASE_13_PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT.md`
+- `docs/OPERATIONS_RUNBOOK.md`
+- `docs/DISASTER_RECOVERY_RUNBOOK.md`
+- `docs/PHASE_15_LAUNCH_AND_HANDOVER.md`
+
+## Current development line
+
+The published stable release is `v1.0.1`. Ongoing product-completion work is tracked under `1.1.0-dev` and is described in `docs/PHASE_16_COMPLETION_AUDIT.md` and `docs/PRODUCT_COMPLETION_ROADMAP.md`.
+
+## Security
+
+Report security issues according to `SECURITY.md`. Never post credentials, tokens, private keys, `.env` files, or production data in public issues or chat messages.
+
+## License
+
+Proprietary. See `LICENSE.md`.
