@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Phase 16 — Product Completion Audit
+
+## Audit basis
+
+The audit reviewed the `v1.0.1` source tree at commit `4e364f61dfaba827cbfee679230e6843104b41ea`.
+
+## What is already strong
+
+- Event-driven modular-monolith backend with explicit tenancy boundaries
+- Identity, RBAC, 2FA, passkeys, session and device tracking
+- Double-entry wallet and deposit settlement
+- Commerce, supplier routing, rules, fraud and dynamic pricing
+- SaaS entitlements, plugins, analytics and reconciliation
+- Notifications, webhooks, support, reports, invoices and reliability controls
+- Automated backend regression tests and frontend static checks
+- Docker-based local and production topologies
+
+## Blocking gaps before production deployment
+
+1. Release hygiene and version metadata were inconsistent.
+2. The tracked source tree still contained temporary hotfix, patch and backup artifacts.
+3. `.env.production.example` existed locally but was ignored and absent from the release archive.
+4. The root README described an old Phase 11 hotfix instead of the platform.
+5. Dependency lockfiles are missing, so builds are not reproducible.
+6. The security workflow watches `main`, while the active branch is `master`.
+7. Live payment, supplier, SMTP/SMS/push integrations are not connected.
+8. Customer-facing legal, account-profile and full email-verification experiences are incomplete.
+9. Physical-commerce shipping addresses, delivery methods and shipment tracking are not modeled.
+10. Frontend unit/E2E/accessibility coverage and backend static-analysis coverage are absent.
+
+## Phase 16A result
+
+This cleanup patch:
+
+- replaces the root README;
+- begins the `1.1.0-dev` completion line;
+- aligns version metadata;
+- tracks a sanitized production environment template;
+- removes obsolete top-level repair artifacts and stale backup files;
+- expands ignore rules for future generated backups;
+- updates the security workflow to run on both `master` and `main`;
+- adds the completion roadmap.
+
+## Remaining work
+
+See `docs/PRODUCT_COMPLETION_ROADMAP.md`.
